	(text "SAM dedicated switch inputs, harness compatible with the SAM CPU board (520-5246) J2, J3 and J13 (KK-396, 3.96 mm).\nPin order follows the SAM CPU board schematic in this repository (hardware/kicad/sam_cpu, sw_dedicated_1/2): check it with a meter.\nRouted: J3 D9-D16 (flipper buttons and EOS), J13 D17-D24 (tilt, slam, ticket notch, D20, BACK, MINUS, PLUS, SELECT)\nand J2 pin 10 (coin door memory protect). Not routed: J2 D1-D8 (coin slots), key pins.\nPer input: 1 k pull-up to +3.3 V (about 3.3 mA wetting current, the original uses 1.5 k to 4.5 V),\n10 k series and 1 nF (10 us) to the RP2354B. Switch closed = low. No 5 V reaches the MCU.\nTron LE names (rom_data/states/dedicated_switches.csv): D9 L flipper, D10 L EOS, D11 R flipper, D12 R EOS, D13 UL flipper,\nD17 tilt, D18 slam, D19 ticket notch, D21 BACK, D22 MINUS, D23 PLUS, D24 SELECT. D14-D16 and D20 vary per game."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6484ddb1-e4fa-4a40-abc5-90c10d403bb2")
	)
